    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. There are only 3 test files (the acceptance test plus its two support classes), and the single test class passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required emitting an AUDIT log line on successful owner create, containing the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`.\n\nI made a minimal, single-file change to `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n- Added an `AUDIT` logger (`LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`) as a static field and the two SLF4J imports.\n- Added one line in `addOwner`, right after `saveOwner`, logging the id, customer code, and registration date.\n\n**Why this keeps structural impact low:** the change is confined to a single line inside `addOwner` (cyclomatic complexity 1), and it touches only one file. I deliberately avoided introducing a helper method or a second file \u2014 because the cost model multiplies by the number of files touched, a one-line addition in the single already-relevant method is cheaper than factoring out a new unit. The fields (`customerCode`, `registrationDate`) were already populated at that point (`customerCode` set just above; `registrationDate` defaulted to the current business day by the entity setter), so no other code needed to change.\n\nThe AUDIT output confirms it works: `AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-02`.",
